      "check": "forager full current public/internal text equality",
      "pass": true,
      "actual": "NEW finite interpretation of the source guarantee: in an accessible non-desert, non-arctic area that actually contains enough recoverable edible food and potable water, spend one active eight-hour forage Watch to gather the normal daily food and water requirement for yourself and up to six other ordinary Small/Medium people. This feat guarantees that result from qualifying available resources without a separate yield roll; it does not guarantee access through a hazard, remove contamination or defeat a resource-specific harvesting gate. Identify a real foraging area and deplete its recorded stocks. The actual expedition procedure supplies food/water units, body-size requirements, carry weight and Supply conversion; this feat creates no extra abstract Supply. Larger or unusual consumers use their actual greater requirement from the same finite quantity, not seven unlimited creature-day portions. Record one feat forage output per holder per24 elapsed hours, shared across all locations, with the window beginning on completion; a second feat owner can work separately only against remaining real stock and their actual time. Deserts and arctic regions use ordinary foraging. A stripped, sealed or foodless place cannot satisfy the prerequisite, and no water appears because food exists. Preserve, transport and consume the actual output normally.\nNEW explicit quantity ceiling: the seven ordinary Small/Medium daily food-and-water portions are at most14lb edible food and56pints potable water in one completed480-active-minute Watch. Each pint of water is1lb for the existing cargo accounting. A Large consumer normally uses4lb/16pints from this same stock. These are food/water only, not seven complete Supply Units: no oil, sundries, storage or transport is awarded. If the full guarantee cannot be supported, before work declare an ordinary lawful forage attempt or a smaller supported quantity under this feat; its no-yield-roll benefit may recover only that predeclared real accessible amount. The one-completion/24-elapsed-hour and all actual acquisition/handling restrictions still apply.",
      "expected": "NEW finite interpretation of the source guarantee: in an accessible non-desert, non-arctic area that actually contains enough recoverable edible food and potable water, spend one active eight-hour forage Watch to gather the normal daily food and water requirement for yourself and up to six other ordinary Small/Medium people. This feat guarantees that result from qualifying available resources without a separate yield roll; it does not guarantee access through a hazard, remove contamination or defeat a resource-specific harvesting gate. Identify a real foraging area and deplete its recorded stocks. The actual expedition procedure supplies food/water units, body-size requirements, carry weight and Supply conversion; this feat creates no extra abstract Supply. Larger or unusual consumers use their actual greater requirement from the same finite quantity, not seven unlimited creature-day portions. Record one feat forage output per holder per24 elapsed hours, shared across all locations, with the window beginning on completion; a second feat owner can work separately only against remaining real stock and their actual time. Deserts and arctic regions use ordinary foraging. A stripped, sealed or foodless place cannot satisfy the prerequisite, and no water appears because food exists. Preserve, transport and consume the actual output normally.\nNEW explicit quantity ceiling: the seven ordinary Small/Medium daily food-and-water portions are at most14lb edible food and56pints potable water in one completed480-active-minute Watch. Each pint of water is1lb for the existing cargo accounting. A Large consumer normally uses4lb/16pints from this same stock. These are food/water only, not seven complete Supply Units: no oil, sundries, storage or transport is awarded. If the full guarantee cannot be supported, before work declare an ordinary lawful forage attempt or a smaller supported quantity under this feat; its no-yield-roll benefit may recover only that predeclared real accessible amount. The one-completion/24-elapsed-hour and all actual acquisition/handling restrictions still apply."
